From e1049f326b172c40f5c0e6bf649e4b9345c589bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chatgptyukkuri <chatgptyukkuri@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:48:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] vkd3d-shader/fx: Track the location of each component
 of fx_2_0 expression values.

The components of a value don't need to be stored in consecutive registers
any more. Swizzles and casts which don't change the value no longer need any
instruction, and instructions are split when their operands are not
consecutive. This will allow writing values that don't fit in a single
register, such as matrices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkAyMz3ChWUcwV1bWoNa1Z
